    "mission_1.hallway_analysis": "The curved motion could confuse or discomfort someone nearby because the robot is continuously changing direction while moving forward, making its movement unpredictable than straight motion. I would reduce the angular velocity to make the turn more gradual. The trade off is that the robot would need more time and distance to complete the same distance.\n\nOne safety criterion for acceptable motion around people would be maintaining a minimum passing distance, such as at least 1 meter from a person. This could be evaluated by recording the robot's and person's positions during a trial and measuring the minimum distance between them. The motion could be considered okay if the robot maintains at least the required distance throughout the entire movement and gives the person enough time to respond.",
    "mission_1.predictions": {
